  "result": "Subcommand contexts now get their own entry from the parent's `default_map`, so nested maps like `{\"sub\": {\"opt\": \"x\"}}` take effect. The full suite passes: 1908 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. I didn't run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't confirmed they fail without the fix.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/click/core.py:392` now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. A subcommand with no matching key gets no defaults and falls back to the option's own default.\n- **Tests:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` and `test_default_map_nested_groups` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. The first covers both a subcommand with an entry and one without; the second covers a two-level group.\n- **Docs:** the `default_map` parameter docstring now describes the nested lookup. I added a `CHANGES.md` entry under a new \"Version 8.5.1 \u2013 Unreleased\" heading; I made up that version number, since 8.5.0 is already marked released.",
